WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.037
A running total uses an accumulator—a variable that starts with an initial value and is updated during each repetition.

00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:15.972
Total begins at zero. The loop adds one hundred, then two hundred, then one hundred fifty.

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:21.890
The running values become one hundred, three hundred, and finally four hundred fifty.

00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:24.738
This pattern is extremely common.

00:00:24.738 --> 00:00:33.865
Counters, sums, running balances, and category totals all use the same basic idea: initialize, update, finish.
